1
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:26,000
Sometimes to find yourself you need to get a little lost.

2
00:12:40,000 --> 00:12:46,000
Hector and the Search for Happiness is a adventure,
drama, comedy film directed by Peter Chelsom.

3
00:19:00,000 --> 00:19:06,000
Hector is a quirky psychiatrist who has become
increasingly tired of his humdrum life.

4
00:25:20,000 --> 00:25:26,000
As he tells his girlfriend, Clara, he feels like a fraud: he hasn’t really tasted life, and
yet he’s offering advice to patients who are just not getting any happier.

5
00:31:40,000 --> 00:31:46,000
So Hector decides to break out of his deluded and routine driven life.

6
00:38:00,000 --> 00:38:06,000
Armed with buckets of courage and child-like curiosity, he embarks on a global quest
in hopes of uncovering the elusive secret formula for true happiness.

7
00:44:20,000 --> 00:44:26,000
And so begins a larger than life adventure with riotously funny results.

8
00:50:40,000 --> 00:50:46,000
Hector, played by Simon Pegg.

9
00:57:00,000 --> 00:57:06,000
Clara, played by Rosamund Pike.

10
01:03:20,000 --> 01:03:26,000
Agnes, played by Toni Collette.

11
01:09:40,000 --> 01:09:46,000
Edward, played by Stellan Skarsgård.

12
01:16:00,000 --> 01:16:06,000
Professor Coreman, played by Christopher Plummer.

13
01:22:20,000 --> 01:22:26,000
Diego Baresco, played by Jean Reno.

14
01:28:40,000 --> 01:28:46,000
Hector and the Search for Happiness is a 2014 comedy-drama film directed by Peter Chelsom and co-written by
Chelsom with Tinker Lindsay and Maria von Heland, based on François Lelord's novel of the same name.

15
01:35:00,000 --> 01:35:06,000
The film stars Simon Pegg as Hector and Rosamund Pike as Clara.

16
01:41:20,000 --> 01:41:26,000
The film explores themes of china, africa, routine, narration, office.

17
01:47:40,000 --> 01:47:46,000
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
